  "voice_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172652_b9a5ed5f-d286-47b7-b11d-921613ca695d.mp3",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "Why do credit cards have sixteen digits? They are not random. Every single digit has a job, starting with the very first one.",
      "image_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172800_8929bbb3-d969-4d1b-82d3-3b814be6a629.png",
      "motion_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_173026_939635c2-ca3b-4673-a890-546495083b3e.mp4"
    },
    {
      "text": "A four means Visa, a five usually means Mastercard. The first six to eight digits name the bank that issued your card.",
      "image_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172800_ded79a93-dcf0-4e53-a1ee-8bf7491c2f40.png",
      "motion_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_173025_082eb6cf-d9fb-4eab-820a-bdc12433ee0f.mp4"
    },
    {
      "text": "The middle digits are your account, and the final digit is a math check that catches typos. Next time someone asks you",
      "image_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172801_db0b4b5b-f993-488e-bf49-317c2e3b30f1.png",
      "motion_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_173026_ca5307d1-f16c-4a66-97e5-3888259c0eb5.mp4"
    }
  ]
}
